Text:
@hungry_40 @waka_dai_shou_ 有り難う御座います🙇‍♂️！
試作品を作っている時に濃度を3種類作ったのですが、タイ人は薄いスープでファラン真ん中で自分は濃いのが好みでした😅
濃度が0.5%違うだけで全然変わっちゃうから面白いです😊🍜

translated_Text:
@hungry_40 @waka_dai_shou_ Thank you 🙇‍♂️!
I made three different concentrations while making the prototype, but Thai people prefer a thin soup in the middle of the Faran and thicker ones 😅
It's interesting because just a 0.5% difference in concentration can completely change 😊🍜

Text:
@hungry_40 @waka_dai_shou_ うちは灰汁出しは硬水の水道水で、スープはRO水と言う超軟水を使っています。
味玉の漬けタレを作る時にも使用しますが、鰹節や昆布でも明らかに差が出ますね。
まだまだ良い方法があるとは思うのですが手探り状態です😅

translated_Text:
@hungry_40 @waka_dai_shou_ We use hard water tap water to remove lye, and we use ultra soft water called RO water for the soup.
It is also used to make pickled sauce with seasoned eggs, but there are clearly differences between bonito flakes and kelp.
I think there's still a better way to do it, but I'm groping

